<div>
    <h4>Pre-flight checklist</h4>
    <ol>
        <li>Activate <strong>FEEDWATER</strong> valve.</li>
        <li>Activate coolant pumps <strong>ALPHA</strong> and <strong>BETA</strong>.</li>
        <li>Optionally, activate <strong>COOLANT</strong> valve</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div>
    <h4>Startup</h4>
    <ol>
        <li>In the Shift Manager section, activate <strong>BRAVO-8</strong>.</li>
        <li>In the STARTUP section, activate <strong>SHUTDOWN PUMPS</strong></li>
        <li>Press the <strong>REACTOR IGNITION</strong> red button.</li>
        <li>Once the temperature heats up to <strong>650K</strong>, <strong>raise</strong> the control rods to <strong>55%</strong>
            to stabilize the temperature.
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div>
    <h4>Turbine syncing</h4>

    <p>Repeat the following steps for both Turbine 1 and Turbine 2.</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Get the reactor temperature to around <strong>1420K</strong>.<br/>You can close the <strong>COOLANT</strong>
            valve until the desired temperature is reached.
        </li>
        <li>Open the valve of the turbine to reach <strong>3.61 m<sup>3</sup>/s</strong> of flowrate.</li>
        <li>Set the acceleration switch to <strong>F</strong> until around <strong>2970 RPM</strong>, then set
            acceleration to <strong>S</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>When the RPM gets closer to <strong>3000</strong>, it should be slow enough to easily sync the turbine.<br/>At
            this point, when the light lands on the <strong>green dot</strong>, press the <strong>SYNC</strong> switch.
        </li>
        <li>Increase the flow rate to start producing power, this will be your main way to complete power orders.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div>
    <h4>Power orders</h4>

    <ol>
        <li>Enable the power orders by switching on the <strong>ENABLE ORDERS</strong> switch.</li>
        <li>When available, the <strong>DEMAND</strong> will be displayed on the top side of screen.</li>
        <li>Use the turbines flow valve to match the power output to the demand.</li>
    </ol>
</div>